\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {How much authority should the neural component have?} Hazard-identification accuracy on the same 19 SafeLIBERO scenes, grouped by what the VLM is asked to do. Letting it \emph  {decide the scene} (grey) or \emph  {compose the rule} (orange) is worse than restricting it to \emph  {grounding predicates} that a fixed rule composes (blue). Light extensions are the deployed top-2 guard set. The ordering, not any single bar, is the finding.}}{10}{figure.7}}
\newlabel{fig:vlmauth}{{7}{10}{\textbf {How much authority should the neural component have?} Hazard-identification accuracy on the same 19 SafeLIBERO scenes, grouped by what the VLM is asked to do. Letting it \emph {decide the scene} (grey) or \emph {compose the rule} (orange) is worse than restricting it to \emph {grounding predicates} that a fixed rule composes (blue). Light extensions are the deployed top-2 guard set. The ordering, not any single bar, is the finding}{figure.7}{}}
